  "source_contract_review": [
    {
      "area": "Reset commit",
      "finding": "invalidate(reset) still advances the finite bus/control epoch, discards staged address/control admission and begins existing request drains without revoking loans. reset_pending remains until all selected request pointers detach, bounded hot TX/RX flushes succeed, every selected halt/PID observation passes, and DCFG address clearing is read back exactly. Only that commit clears software halted, snapshot.address, setup_pending and reset_pending."
    },
    {
      "area": "DCFG readback",
      "finding": "The write preserves all DCFG bits outside address mask0x7F0, executes DSB and compares exact register readback. Refusal preserves the old snapshot address/reset gate/clock duty. New submit rejectsSTATE with request stillREADY; service retries after the external fault is lifted. A write attempt alone never publishes address0 or reopens admission."
    },
    {
      "area": "STALL and bulk DATA0",
      "finding": "clear_halts is bounded by the validated maximum8 selected directions. It clears STALL and requests SD0PID only for bulk non-EP0, then reads actual STALL21 and DPID16. Partial earlier hardware success does not publish partial software-halt clearance: the global reset gate remains until every direction and DCFG prove safe. EP0 never receives reserved SD0/SD1 commands."
    },
    {
      "area": "Enabled selected direction without a loan",
      "finding": "During reset an observed enabled IN0/bulkIN/nonzeroOUT prevents halt/PID restoration and reset commit even when its software request isNULL. The controller retains clock/reset duty instead of adopting or overwriting the unexplained source. OUT0 is exempt because internal SETUP reception is armed without an application buffer. This proof concerns selected directions, not arbitrary unconfigured hardware inventory."
    },
    {
      "area": "SETUP recovery",
      "finding": "setup_pending clears and both software EP0 halt flags reset only after both EP0 request pointers areNULL and both hardware STALL-clear readbacks succeed. Bus reset takes precedence. A refused IN or OUT0 STALL clear blocks control admission without borrowing candidate storage; service retries in the same epoch."
    },
    {
      "area": "Global OUT NAK",
      "finding": "progress no longer emits clear-global-OUT-NAK while reset_pending. Thus a previously observed NAK remains asserted after an OUT loan has actually drained if address/halt reset proof still fails, then normal NAK clearing resumes after commit. This preserves observed NAK; it does not establish an unconditional new SGONAK-acquisition protocol for all idle resets."
    },
    {
      "area": "Per-loan proof versus global reset duty",
      "finding": "An endpoint loan may SETTLE after its own real disable/NAK/FIFO/RX-status/W1C withdrawal proof while DCFG/another halt still blocks overall reset. That is independent proved request completion, not reset-induced revocation. Pointer detach precedes nx_request_settle, still the final request access. Unproved drain remains DRAINING thenQUARANTINED with storage/clock retained until actual progress or joined stop."
    },
    {
      "area": "Stop and hot-path cost",
      "finding": "Existing stop still proves disconnect/globalNAK, endpoints/FIFO, source/NVIC disable, publisher join and clock release; OUT0 fixed EPD behavior is unchanged. New helper adds only bounded local loop/MMIO work, no allocation/registry/dispatch layer or persistent controller state. Actual code-size/latency cost was not measured."
    }
  ],
